@startuml 01d-comparison
title Docker vs Podman build paths — deployment comparison

skinparam defaultFontName Menlo
skinparam component {
    BackgroundColor #FAFAFA
    BorderColor Black
}

left to right direction

package "Host (operator's laptop)" {
    folder "ivaliceCluster/" as Repo {
        [scripts/build.sh] as Build
        [scripts/_pigen-podman.sh] as Helper
        [configs/config.base] as Config
        folder "stages/" as Stages
        folder "assets/" as Assets
        folder "pi-gen/\n(upstream submodule)" as PiGen
        folder "pi-gen/deploy/" as Deploy
    }
}

package "Stock Docker path (NOT used)" #FFF0F0 {
    [pi-gen/build-docker.sh\n(upstream)] as BD
    [Docker daemon] as DD
    component "pi-gen container\n(Docker)" as ContainerD {
        note top of ContainerD : bind: /config only\nmissing: /stages, /assets
    }
}

package "ivaliceCluster Podman path (current)" #F0FFF0 {
    [scripts/_pigen-podman.sh\nrun_pigen()] as RP
    [podman-machine VM\n(macOS)] as VM
    [podman] as P
    component "pi-gen container\n(Podman, privileged)" as ContainerP {
        note top of ContainerP : bind: /config, /stages, /assets\nfull ivaliceCluster tree visible
    }
}

Build --> Helper
Build --> Config
Helper --> RP : run_pigen(config)

' Docker path (shown for contrast)
RP .[#gray].> BD : NOT used
BD .[#gray].> DD
DD .[#gray].> ContainerD
ContainerD .[#gray].> Deploy : no custom stages →\nimage lacks Ivalice rootfs

' Podman path (actual)
RP --> VM : clear stale loops\n(ssh + losetup -d)
RP --> P : podman build\npodman run
P --> ContainerP
ContainerP --> PiGen : read stages + Dockerfile
ContainerP --> Stages : /stages (bind)
ContainerP --> Assets : /assets (bind)
ContainerP --> Deploy : write *.img

note right of BD
  **Why stock Docker path is unsuitable:**
  1. build-docker.sh's "rootless" grep misfires
     against rootful podman info.
  2. Only bind-mounts the config file; our stages
     and assets live outside pi-gen/.
  3. No hook to clear podman-machine stale loop
     devices or patch util-linux 2.41 losetup -f.
end note

note right of ContainerP
  **Why Podman path works:**
  - Three bind mounts expose the whole
    ivaliceCluster tree.
  - Helper script enforces rootful mode
    on macOS and cleans the VM kernel
    state before build.
  - Patches pi-gen/scripts/common for the
    util-linux 2.41 losetup -f annotation
    before `podman build` bakes it in.
end note

@enduml
